delayMinMinutes.description:
DEPRECATED: holds SECONDS despite the name. Writes EM_CAMPAIGN.DelayMin raw, which the scheduler consumes as seconds;
the earlier "in minutes" description was wrong. Use delayMinSeconds instead, which takes precedence when both are sent;
this field will be removed in v3. Not to be confused with the sender resource's delayMinMinutes, which genuinely holds
minutes.

